NEARS-1811 QA finding: Arabic content-desc collision on OrderDetailsScreen (order #91132, ar locale)

Command:
python3 scripts/app-nav/uifind.py find "تتبع الطلب" --exact  (on Admin/UserApp order_details_screen, ar locale, order #91132, pending)

Output (verbatim):
uifind: emulator-5554 dumped 17382 bytes from /sdcard/uinav-fe4e8cf267484ad8b8572fdd615693f0.xml; parsed 44 node(s), 27 labelled
AMBIGUOUS: "تتبع الطلب" matched 2 distinct nodes (use --first to accept any, or a more specific label):
  label="تتبع الطلب"  clickable=true  area=21609  at 115,1830
  label="تتبع الطلب"  clickable=false  area=81672  at 540,319
rc=3

Root cause: two DIFFERENT translation keys resolve to the IDENTICAL Arabic string.
  UserApp/assets/language/ar.json:151  "track_order": "تتبع الطلب"      <- the FAB tooltip added by this ticket (order_details_screen.dart:254)
  UserApp/assets/language/ar.json:335  "order_tracking": "تتبع الطلب"   <- the pre-existing "Order Tracking" section heading (order_status_hero_widget.dart:51)
English values are distinct ("Track Order" vs "Order Tracking") so this collision is Arabic-only.
  UserApp/assets/language/en.json:176  "track_order": "Track Order"
  UserApp/assets/language/en.json:359  "order_tracking": "Order Tracking"

Effect: before this fix the FAB had NO a11y label at all, so no collision existed (the heading was the
only "تتبع الطلب" node). This fix newly attaches an accessible label to the FAB using the SAME visible
string the pre-existing heading already carries in ar -- so an Arabic screen-reader/automation user
now hears/matches "تتبع الطلب" for BOTH the non-interactive heading (clickable=false) and the actual
track-order FAB (clickable=true), and cannot disambiguate by label alone. This directly breaks the QA
Test Scope requirement: "ui_find on ... localized ar ... strings on OrderDetailsScreen -> rc=0 unique"
-- Arabic returns rc=3 AMBIGUOUS, not rc=0 unique.

bn/es checked via translation-file static read: both keys resolve to DISTINCT strings in bn.json and
es.json (bn: "ট্র্যাক অর্ডার " vs "অর্ডার ট্র্যাকিং"; es: "Seguimiento del pedido" vs "Seguimiento de pedidos")
-- no collision in those locales.
